			<item>
				<title>How to write an Interactive story</title>
				<link>https://vaclavblazej.github.io/post/2022/storytelling/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 09 Jan 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://vaclavblazej.github.io/post/2022/storytelling/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;This is an old version of the post about interactive stories, which I didn&amp;rsquo;t quite finish.&#xA;Please have a look at the &lt;a href=&#34;https://vaclavblazej.github.io/post/2024/interactive_stories&#34;&gt;newer version&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expandbox&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expand-container hidden&#34; id=&#34;0_programmer-box&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;button class=&#34;expand-title&#34; id=&#34;0_programmer-control&#34;&gt;➤ &lt;b&gt;I&amp;#39;m a programmer, not a writer :o&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expand-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If I were a pure writer, then I couldn&amp;rsquo;t explain the target concepts.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you are a programmer, then this post will be easier for you to read because it tries to convey basic programming concepts with comprehensible words and many examples.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you are not a programmer, then this post was meant for you :)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Imagemagick examples</title>
				<link>https://vaclavblazej.github.io/post/2021/imagemagick/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 22 Apr 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://vaclavblazej.github.io/post/2021/imagemagick/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;The imagemagick&amp;rsquo;s magick (convert) program provides a great command line tool for editing images.&#xA;Doing a simple bulk edition can be frustrating as there are many unuseful resources for this program.&#xA;I made this page to keep examples of most useful commands I needed, found, and used.&#xA;It is written in a way so that when read sequentially you should get a reasonable idea how to use this tool.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expandbox&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expand-container hidden&#34; id=&#34;bash-box&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;button class=&#34;expand-title&#34; id=&#34;bash-control&#34;&gt;➤ &lt;b&gt;Running bulk commands&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;expand-content&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To be able to do bulk edition a basic &lt;code&gt;bash&lt;/code&gt; knowledge is expected.&#xA;A command similar to the following one is expected to be used with the commands.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;background-color:#f7f7f7;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-bash&#34; data-lang=&#34;bash&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cf222e&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; i in folder/*.png&lt;span style=&#34;color:#1f2328&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#cf222e&#34;&gt;do&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    convert &lt;span style=&#34;color:#953800&#34;&gt;$i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#0a3069&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cf222e&#34;&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;dirname &lt;span style=&#34;color:#0a3069&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#953800&#34;&gt;$i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#0a3069&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cf222e&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#0a3069&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cf222e&#34;&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;basename &lt;span style=&#34;color:#0a3069&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#953800&#34;&gt;$i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#0a3069&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt; .png&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cf222e&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#0a3069&#34;&gt;.bmp&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#cf222e&#34;&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
			</item>
